\subsection{Error pages and rejected answers}

The lecturer-only routes used to build their refusal from a subject and
a shared tail (\enquote{Results pages are} \ldots{} \enquote{only
available on localhost}).  A translation cannot be glued together that
way, since the verb and its agreement move, so each route has a whole
sentence.  \enquote{Localhost} becomes \enquote{lokalt på servern}, the
place a respondent can understand.

A rejected answer names what was wrong with it, so the parser's
reasons are messages too.  Only a request no form would send (a crafted
body, a number that is not one) gets the generic
[[answer.unreadable]].

